\description{
The structural, trait-based model: the phenotype of a plant responds to the
phenotypes of its neighbours,
\deqn{y = M y + X b + \sum_k Z_k u_k + e, \qquad
  M_{(t,i),(u,j)} = \Psi_{tu} W_t[i, j],}{y = M y + X b + sum_k Z_k u_k + e,  M[(t,i),(u,j)] = Psi[t,u] W_t[i,j],}
with \code{Psi[t, u]} the effect of trait \code{u} of a neighbour (emitter, column) on
trait \code{t} of the focal plant (receiver, row). With \code{A = I - M} invertible,
\verb{y* = A y} follows the ordinary model of the package, so every term and
residual structure applies to it unchanged; only the objective changes.
}
\details{
\strong{Parameters.} The free entries of \code{Psi} come last in \code{theta}, receiver by
receiver, named \code{Psi[receiver<-emitter]}. Internally they are scaled by the
mean absolute row sum \code{s} of \code{W} (\verb{theta = Psi s}, the effect of the whole
neighbourhood), so that they share the scale of the variance parameters;
outputs are in units of \code{W}. Standard errors come from the same observed
Hessian as those of the variance components.

\strong{log|det A|.} Three exact paths, chosen once from the structure: when the
possible non-zero pattern of \code{Psi} has no cycle (no feedback, e.g. only
\code{T2 <- T1}), \verb{det A = 1}; with one symmetric \code{W} and every \verb{(trait, unit)}
observed once, \verb{log|det A| = sum_k log det(I_q - lambda_k Psi)} over the
eigenvalues \code{lambda_k} of \code{W}, computed once; otherwise a dense LU of \code{A}.

\strong{Admissible region.} Every real eigenvalue of \code{M} must be below 1, i.e.
\verb{det(I - t M) > 0} for all \code{t} in \verb{(0, 1]}: the region reached from
\code{Psi = 0} without crossing a singular \code{A}. Outside it the objective returns
a large finite penalty, so that the line search backtracks. The condition is
checked exactly at every evaluation on the eigenvalue path; on the general
path only \verb{det A > 0} is checked during the fit and the exact condition at
the end (\code{fit$lag$admissible}). The spectral radius of \code{M} is reported; a
value above 1 with all real eigenvalues below 1 is allowed (the simultaneous
model is defined, the equilibrium is no longer the limit of iterating
\verb{y <- M y + ...}). For one trait the region is the usual parameter space of
the SAR model, \code{psi} in \verb{(1/lambda_min, 1/lambda_max)}; for several traits it
contains the stability region \verb{rho(Psi) rho(W) < 1} and is larger than it.

\strong{Masks.} With a plant term carrying an indirect environmental effect
(incidence \code{W} placed on a trait, IEE*), the plant level of the structural
model is VP+ in other coordinates: with both \code{Psi[t,u]} and \code{Psi[u,t]} free,
the direction of transmission is only weakly identified, and \code{\link[=rx_model]{rx_model()}}
warns. Leave at most one of each reciprocal pair free (\code{struct = "mask"},
\code{receivers}, \code{emitters}). Without IEE*, \code{Psi} is identified when full,
through the genetic level, at a cost in precision.

\strong{Not available} with a lag: the sparse engine, Kenward-Roger, predict and
the genome scan.
